meta {
  name: Rewrite Policy
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/policies/{{soldPolicyId}}/rewrite
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // Allstate policy numbers are digits only, and a policy number is unique per
  // agency — so a fixed literal here books once and then collides forever.
  bru.setVar("rewritePolicyNumber", String(Date.now()).slice(-9));
}

body:json {
  {
    "cancelledAt": "2026-03-10",
    "policies": [
      {
        "policyType": "Auto",
        "effectiveDate": "2026-03-15",
        "carrier": "Allstate",
        "policyNumber": "{{rewritePolicyNumber}}",
        "premium": 1050,
        "itemCount": 1,
        "newBusinessApplication": {
          "key": "{{rewriteDocumentKey}}",
          "filename": "rewrite-application.pdf",
          "contentType": "application/pdf",
          "size": 2048
        }
      }
    ],
    "submissionToken": "{{$guid}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("returns the new deal and the cancelled policy", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("dealId");
    expect(body.cancelledPolicyId).to.equal(bru.getVar("soldPolicyId"));
    expect(body.retiredStatus).to.equal("Cancel Rewrite");
  });

  test("reports what the cancellation cost", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    // Always the cancelled policy's premium, in both branches.
    expect(body.chargebackAmount).to.be.a("number");
    expect(body.chargebackAmount).to.be.at.least(0);
    expect(body).to.have.property("withinClawbackWindow");
    // Signed: `-chargebackAmount` inside the window, 0 outside it. Never
    // positive — a rewrite cannot *add* credit to the original sale.
    expect(body.soldAdjustment).to.be.at.most(0);
    if (body.withinClawbackWindow) {
      expect(body.soldAdjustment).to.equal(-body.chargebackAmount);
    } else {
      expect(body.soldAdjustment).to.equal(0);
    }
  });

  test("captures the replacement for the history request", function () {
    bru.setVar("rewriteDealId", res.getBody().dealId);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /policies/:id/rewrite — cancel a policy and book its replacement

  Module `deal_audits`, permission **`deal_audits:write`**. Data scope is
  enforced by `loadOwnedPolicy`, the same clamp `PATCH /policies/:id` uses: a
  policy outside the caller's scope 404s rather than 403s, and under `own` scope
  a policy with no deal is unattributable and therefore out of scope.

  ## What it does, in one transaction

  1. Retires the policy named in the URL — `active: false`, status
     **`Cancel Rewrite`** — and points `transferredToPolicyId` at its
     replacement.
  2. Writes the replacement policies on a **new deal**, booked
     `businessType: "new_business"`. A rewrite is a real sale, unlike a Company
     Transfer.
  3. Writes one row to the `chargebacks` ledger and, inside the clawback window,
     `$inc`s the **original** deal's `chargebackAdjustment`.

  This is the only way a policy's status becomes `Cancel Rewrite`.
  `PATCH /policies/:id` rejects that status with a 400, because the product rule
  is that a policy cannot be Cancel Rewrite without the policy that replaced it.

  ## The money

  | When the policy was cancelled | Chargeback | Producer's sold figure |
  |---|---|---|
  | Within 1 calendar month of the **original deal's sold date** | Full premium | Reduced by the premium |
  | After that | Full premium | Unchanged |

  The window is measured in whole calendar months at day granularity, and the
  boundary day is inside it — a deal sold 10 March is within the window until and
  including 10 April. The premium is used as the charged-back amount because the
  system records no payment or down-payment figure.

  ## Body

  | Field | Type | Req | Notes |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `cancelledAt` | `YYYY-MM-DD` | yes | The date the window is judged against, and the replacement deal's sold date. Clamped server-side to never be in the future nor before the original sale. |
  | `policies[]` | array(1–10) | yes | Replacement policies. Validated by the same `policyBaseSchema` the Sold form and the transfer use — carrier, policy number format, premium, item count, signed application, discounts. **No `fromPolicyId`**: the cancelled policy is the URL. Prior insurance and cancellation are injected as "none" and must not be sent. |
  | `submissionToken` | string | no | Makes a retry idempotent. Namespaced `RWRT\|…` server-side, so it cannot collide with a sold or transfer token. |

  ⚠ **Document keys must come from `POST :id/rewrite/presign`** (seq 3), not from
  the sold or transfer presign. Rewrite attachments are verified against the
  `policy-rewrites/<householdId>` purpose, so a key minted under another flow's
  prefix fails `assertKeyOwnership` with a 400.

  More than one replacement row is allowed: only the first is linked to the
  cancelled policy, and the rest are ordinary new policies on the same deal — the
  case where one Auto becomes an Auto plus a Motorcycle.

  ## Response `201`

  ```json
  {
    "dealId": "...",
    "cancelledPolicyId": "...",
    "chargebackAmount": 940,
    "soldAdjustment": -940,
    "withinClawbackWindow": true,
    "cancelledAt": "2026-03-10T00:00:00.000Z",
    "retiredStatus": "Cancel Rewrite"
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  | Code | When |
  |---|---|
  | `400` | The policy has no household (the replacement has nowhere to live); or the body fails validation. |
  | `403` | Caller lacks `deal_audits:write`, or the module is disabled for the agency. |
  | `404` | No such policy, or it is outside the caller's data scope. |
  | `409` | The policy is not active, or it has already been replaced — rewrite its replacement instead. |
}
